\label{thm:main}
  Let $\eta>1$ be the fundamental unit of the real quadratic field $L$, let
  $k\in\mathbb{N}$ and define $\rho:=\lfloor k/2\rfloor$. Then, for $X\geq 2$,
  \begin{equation*}
    \NLk(X)= c_k\left(\frac{2\log X}{\log\eta}\right)^\rho+O_{k,L}((\log X)^{\rho-1}),
  \end{equation*}
  where
  \begin{equation*}
    c_k=
    \begin{cases}
      1/\rho! &\text{ if $k$ is even,}\\
      3/\rho! &\text{ if $k$ is odd.}
    \end{cases}
  \end{equation*}

